{"id": 32, "ts": 1780958912.0173004, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f1\u2019s assessment and keep Candidate\u202fC as my provisional recommendation. The panel now has clear evidence that C is 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d covering the core safety\u2011critical criteria of operational reliability, crew cooperation, decision quality, and stress resilience. While C does have communication challenges (difficulty expressing ideas, egocentric style) and a limited willingness for further education, these concerns are comparable to the interpersonal issues we see with B (pretentiousness, occasional wrong tone) and D (hot temper, know\u2011it\u2011all reputation). Moreover, C\u2019s proven ability to foster a positive team environment suggests his communication shortfalls are less likely to impair cockpit teamwork than the memory\u2011for\u2011numbers weakness we know B has, which directly threatens attention and information accuracy. D\u2019s adaptability is hinted at by his \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately\u201d and \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d but we still lack any concrete evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation, and his temperament concerns remain significant. Therefore, Candidate\u202fC still offers the most balanced and safety\u2011critical fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
